xt":"Adam Larsson hit Matvei Gridin","type":{"id":"503","text":"Hit","abbreviation":"hit"},"clock":{"displayValue":"3:34"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"124292"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"2562610","displayName":"Adam Larsson","shortName":"A. Larsson"},"type":"hit-credited"},{"athlete":{"id":"5216897","displayName":"Matvei Gridin","shortName":"M. Gridin"},"type":"hitted"}]},{"id":"401892647000000970","scoringPlay":false,"scoreValue":0,"awayScore":0,"homeScore":0,"text":"Vince Dunn shot blocked by Matvei Gridin","type":{"id":"508","text":"Blocked","abbreviation":"shot-blocked"},"clock":{"displayValue":"3:49"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"3"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"3904189","displayName":"Vince Dunn","shortName":"V. Dunn"},"type":"shooter"},{"athlete":{"id":"5216897","displayName":"Matvei Gridin","shortName":"M. Gridin"},"type":"defender"}]}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"7224","fullName":"Climate Pledge Arena","address":{"city":"Seattle","state":"WA","country":"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/nhl/day/7224.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]}]},"attendance":17151,"officials":[{"fullName":"Jean Hebert","displayName":"Jean Hebert","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Kiel Murchison","displayName":"Kiel Murchison","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Bevan Mills","displayName":"Bevan Mills","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Graedy Hamilton","displayName":"Graedy Hamilton","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Matty Beniers lifts Kraken past Flames 2-1 in overtime","description":"— Matty Beniers scored in overtime and Joey Daccord made 25 saves as the Seattle Kraken beat the Calgary Flames 2-1 on Wednesday night.","story":"SEATTLE -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4781552/matty-beniers\">Matty Beniers</a> scored in overtime and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3942073/joey-daccord\">Joey Daccord</a> made 25 saves as the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/sea/seattle-kraken\">Seattle Kraken</a> beat the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/cgy/calgary-flames\">Calgary Flames</a> 2-1 on Wednesday night.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5216877/berkly-catton\">Berkly Catton</a> also scored for the Kraken (9-5-1), giving him points in seven consecutive games. Beniers’ goal came on a breakaway just 55 seconds into overtime.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4587843/yegor-sharangovich\">Yegor Sharangovich</a> had the Flames’ (7-8-1) only goal. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4587952/dustin-wolf\">Dustin Wolf</a> stopped 27 shots.\n\n\r\n              With 7:45 left in the first period, Sharagovich tipped a slapshot past Daccord. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4312877/zach-whitecloud\">Zach Whitecloud</a> delivered the shot from the blue line.\n\n\r\n              A successful offside challenge by Calgary nullified what would have been a game-tying goal by Catton with 5:11 remaining in the period. Catton redeemed himself with 6:51 left in the second, beating Wolf high.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4392883/martin-pospisil\">Martin Pospisil</a> took his second goaltender interference penalty with 9:11 to go in the game when he ran into Daccord, attempting to play the puck behind his net. The collision left both players sprawled on the ice. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3115032/brandon-montour\">Brandon Montour</a> shoved Pospisil in retaliation. Both players earned roughing penalties.\n\n\r\n              Seattle bounced back after a 6-2 loss against Calgary on Oct. 30. The loss is the Flames’ first in overtime this season.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5149189/matthew-wood\">Matthew Wood</a> made his debut in a Kraken sweater, starting the game alongside <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3067858/chandler-stephenson\">Chandler Stephenson</a> and Freddy Gaudreau, but he failed to record a point. Seattle acquired Wood in exchange for <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5080144/shane-wright\">Shane Wright</a> in a one-for-one swap with the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/nsh/nashville-predators\">Nashville Predators</a> on Nov. 1.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Kraken: Host the Rangers on Saturday.\n\n\r\n              Flames: Host the Ducks on Friday.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-11-05T05:54:35Z"}}